                    {
                        "translation_id": "426d98e0-c9df-4639-8403-b9dd5934f0e2",
                        "source_entry_id": "430dc03c-d489-3fb3-85b6-4aabe1979177",
                        "source_sense_id": "0bcd1bf6-cf7e-3750-8164-8d21b93c684b",
                        "source_sense_description": "een stuk edelgesteente",
                        "target_lang_word": "gem",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gem",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7206ed1-c79a-3c30-9487-57360814428e",
                                        "entry_id": "a89053eb-5650-32cd-9eee-a6d2a530111f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A precious stone, usually of substantial monetary value or prized for its beauty or shine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8473fd7-7338-4e8e-9f81-97ef21cdcd8b",
                                                "sense_id": "d7206ed1-c79a-3c30-9487-57360814428e",
                                                "text": "And on her head she wore a tyre of gold,\nAdornd with gemmes and owches wondrous fayre,\nWhose passing price vneath was to be told;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a529df43-1c91-46ae-b55b-3aae2a9362bb",
                                                "sense_id": "d7206ed1-c79a-3c30-9487-57360814428e",
                                                "text": "Of six preceding ancestors, that gem,\nConferr’d by testament to the sequent issue,\nHath it been owed and worn. This is his wife;\nThat ring’s a thousand proofs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e24f233c-f4d1-424b-a91c-ae5720f1d9fa",
                                                "sense_id": "d7206ed1-c79a-3c30-9487-57360814428e",
                                                "text": "[…] then silent Night\nWith this her solemn Bird and this fair Moon,\nAnd these the Gemms of Heav’n, her starrie train:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12070744-5233-496d-bf52-700d78976566",
                                                "sense_id": "d7206ed1-c79a-3c30-9487-57360814428e",
                                                "text": "Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are diamond, ruby and sapphire, emerald and other gem forms of the mineral beryl, chrysoberyl, tanzanite, tsavorite, topaz and jade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68ee92b9-9639-34a9-8d09-1a5549ed1480",
                                        "entry_id": "a89053eb-5650-32cd-9eee-a6d2a530111f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any precious or highly valued thing or person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9afac358-33c7-45ce-8196-1b3e806fb6f6",
                                                "sense_id": "68ee92b9-9639-34a9-8d09-1a5549ed1480",
                                                "text": "She's an absolute gem."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b2d9ba9-b9f2-4839-9892-fd1ea90ab8f1",
                                                "sense_id": "68ee92b9-9639-34a9-8d09-1a5549ed1480",
                                                "text": "Standout “Hidden Knives” is the kind of new wave-leaning punk gem John Hughes would’ve loved, while “So Beneath You” is a teeth-baring, roiling tune."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d55c04f-ae6a-31b1-8fba-964f427a4a01",
                                        "entry_id": "a89053eb-5650-32cd-9eee-a6d2a530111f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything of small size, or expressed within brief limits, which is regarded as a gem on account of its beauty or value, such as a small picture, a verse of poetry, or an epigram."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b4260a2-da9d-4134-b54a-8e8359e9a404",
                                                "sense_id": "3d55c04f-ae6a-31b1-8fba-964f427a4a01",
                                                "text": "a gem of wit"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c456cd4f-7297-3722-8c95-b39051d6d791",
                                        "entry_id": "a89053eb-5650-32cd-9eee-a6d2a530111f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gemma or leaf bud."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c69a8255-56a7-4c03-b1b1-fa2cf91764b8",
                                                "sense_id": "c456cd4f-7297-3722-8c95-b39051d6d791",
                                                "text": "c. 1668, John Denham (translator), Of Old Age by Cato the Elder, Part 3, in Poems and Translations, with The Sophy, London: H. Herringman, 4th edition, 1773, p. 35,\nThen from the Joynts of thy prolifick Stemm\nA swelling Knot is raised (call’d a Gemm)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d26524b5-90a9-46ad-b9b1-e49a8bc89903",
                                                "sense_id": "c456cd4f-7297-3722-8c95-b39051d6d791",
                                                "text": "Among the crooked Lanes, on every Hedge, / The Glow-Worm lights his Gem […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29217d48-2d7e-491e-b25e-8c66e02e38f8",
                                                "sense_id": "c456cd4f-7297-3722-8c95-b39051d6d791",
                                                "text": "1803, John Browne Cutting, “A Succinct History of Jamaica” in Robert Charles Dallas, The History of the Maroons, London: Longman and Rees, Volume 1, p. xcii,\nIn about twelve days the sprouts from the gems of the planted cane are seen […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ed3b0ce-9907-3a80-9147-e2b51ff69bd7",
                                        "entry_id": "a89053eb-5650-32cd-9eee-a6d2a530111f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A geometrid moth of the species Orthonama obstipata."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
